think Crux-first choice: the card named three candidate next rungs -- a click-then-select-facts read, a marquee-grow read, a codec read. Chose click-then-facts: it closes the click gesture's own loop (click_expand made a group selection; a surface then needs that group's facts) and its crux is the EXACT COMPLEMENT of selection_summary's subset-sharper lesson, the highest-leverage single move.
think Design: image/click_facts.rye joins click_expand (a point -> a whole-group ascending selection) with selection_summary (a selection -> its facts). Verified click_expand returns an ascending dense []u32 that selection_summary accepts. Exposed click_area (0 on miss), click_largest (refuses EmptyClick on miss), click_holed_count (0 on miss), and a ClickFacts bundle read from ONE expansion.
think Scene: reused the proven corner-L chain (A,B corner-Ls, boxes overlap 1-2 and 2-3 yet never 1-3, 8-disconnected) and made C a 5x5 RING (area 16, one hole) so the group's largest and its holed count both differ from any clicked corner-L; a far singleton block D. Worked the ring-in-a-chain geometry: B's box overlaps C's box in (7,7)-(8,8) where B places no pixel while C's border does, so boxes overlap yet pixels stay 3 apart (8-disconnected).
think Crux proven three ways: the click's facts are the group's (click A reads area 34, largest the ring C never clicked, holed 1); any object of a group reads the same facts (A,B,C identical, cross-checked against selection_summary over {1,2,3}); a miss reads zero facts (interior notch -> empty group -> zero area, EmptyClick refused). Plus a singleton's group is itself, off-map refuses PointOutOfBounds, determinism.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no code reds. The only guard catch was one compound assert (`largest >= 1 and largest <= components`) the TAME ban named; split into two named asserts, re-GREEN. Width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, living-docs lint GREEN, living-card ASCII GREEN, 207 image modules.
